		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=2452&amp;p=20369#p20369"><![CDATA[
<blockquote class="uncited"><div>1) How to record the adjusted parameters of the R3TS radio?<br>For example, I have three RT3S radios with OpenGD77 installed. After resetting a radio's settings, how can I import configuration parameters from a configured radio and write the parameter to the reset radio.<br>Is there a way to write radio configuration parameters with OpenGD77 using CPS and save to Codeplug?</div></blockquote><br><br>There is a technical reason why settings are not loaded or saved by the CPS.<br>This is because different versions of the firmware have different settings memory configuations<br><br>Although a function could be written to backup and restore settings, it would fail as soon as new firmware was loaded with any changes to the settings data structure.<br>e.g. New features like GPS enable / disable in the UV380 require changes to the settings data storage.<br><br>Also different radios, have different settings structures because of their different hardware eg. MD9600/UV380/GD77/GD77S/DM1801 etc etc<br><br>So it would never be possible to backup from one type of radio and restore to another.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=50">VK3KYY</a> — Tue Oct 25, 2022 11:18 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
	</entry>
